, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $\\frac{5}{3}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=-\\frac{3}{5}x+12$ has a slope of $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{5})=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=-\\frac{3}{5}x+12$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0073cd82-3474-5411-9100-980c9c8ffaac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514701} {:answer/id #uuid "06212feb-93cf-5320-a368-6a9761c5e90e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{6}x-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514702} {:answer/id #uuid "d92c81c2-ce39-5ca0-98b3-b21a0da0e4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{6}{5}x+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514742} {:answer/id #uuid "f7181426-06a2-573d-97a6-639209f5ccee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{6}x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514747} {:answer/id #uuid "f80758cc-0c4a-514f-aaea-3d2e5dbcbaed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f80758cc-0c4a-514f-aaea-3d2e5dbcbaed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{6}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514748} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae1f790-e520-58c8-a2f4-06a916d6d1db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "806d2bbe-96e2-5d6d-a670-4ccfaeab34a1" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $-10x-12y=-21?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $-10x-12y=-21,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x-12y & =-21 \\\\ -12y & =10x-21 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{10}{12}x+\\frac{21}{12} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{5}{6}x+\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $-\\frac{5}{6}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{6}{5}x+3$ has a slope of $\\frac{6}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{5}{6})\\cdot \\frac{6}{5}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{6}{5}x+3$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a9febaa-84c1-5184-96f6-09b381c7ca95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514711} {:answer/id #uuid "402a1ca3-e9dc-560b-bca6-a8ff47d34ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{9}x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514713} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2560d4-42ed-589b-a70f-98b751d9ac0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{9}{8}x+12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514716} {:answer/id #uuid "6a835dc6-15d6-5d82-a0d5-319758a7aa80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9}{8}x+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514719} {:answer/id #uuid "acac5399-3f1f-5234-b5c8-c4e5c48aeb64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acac5399-3f1f-5234-b5c8-c4e5c48aeb64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514737} :answer-field/id #uuid "716c6c26-c7bd-51ed-93a0-38f6dced205b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c80adf7e-47a6-54d1-b617-5172bdeee1f4" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $-18x-16y=18?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $-18x-16y=18,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18x-16y & =18 \\\\ -16y & =18x+18 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{18}{16}x-\\frac{18}{16} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{9}{8}x-\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $-\\frac{9}{8}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7$ has a slope of $\\frac{8}{9}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{9}{8})\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=\\frac{8}{9}x-7$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "560b5f98-cb98-58a6-98b4-bf241dfb030a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{5}{8}x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514715} {:answer/id #uuid "6064a7af-8df0-5dd7-9b0e-33bb9fa615e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514718} {:answer/id #uuid "6f7ecb44-1bd3-5e97-9d1c-5e976e1bf5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{8}{5}x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514720} {:answer/id #uuid "88aaa3a6-b77c-5219-8e9f-dd2ee93a12ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{5}{8}x+11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514730} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5c6db8-ea53-53f9-9e4f-5a841e917fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6064a7af-8df0-5dd7-9b0e-33bb9fa615e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514718} :answer-field/id #uuid "11304265-79eb-53d3-b36a-ddf025ee509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4a46443-67d5-52dc-a8f6-c15f53d72a9b" :question/problem "Which of the following lines is perpendicular to $-10x+16y=-4?$" :question/worked-solution "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of the given line $-10x+16y=-4,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x+16y & =-4 \\\\ 16y & =10x-4 \\\\ y & =\\frac{10}{16}x-\\frac{4}{16} \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{8}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope of the given line is $\\frac{5}{8}.$\n\nLooking at the answer choices, the line $y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3$ has a slope of $-\\frac{8}{5}.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{5})=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the slopes multiply to $-1,$ we conclude that the line $y=-\\frac{8}{5}x+3$ is perpendicular to the given line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d13b87-15e2-5156-af20-e9f92d7d3e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6ba96fe137b5e6a716ac2f196539a23c783364f3e4ff2fe33384d963760f7cb8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514953} {:answer/id #uuid "37a5d74f-d40f-5fd5-80ec-9ce4a581202b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2e/2e900d35853346bfbbcac7bb7b48298d45dc39313a549c1459b3aefae2834bad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514994} {:answer/id #uuid "426cb82b-e20d-5f97-8a0f-067aa9119d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/df5ae3fe92f747b89e6fdeaad42e4adb8d48db87c302c870caf430442e13cda8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515013} {:answer/id #uuid "95ed6a5f-c6df-523f-b42e-cd835a9a1c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb918b3042ca95c9401f2938258b7f13c909a87d18448c6e36c410a3d092dd94.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515188} {:answer/id #uuid "efcd7883-e1fd-57d5-928e-040cec2366cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e67fd37e421285fcdee0fcd1fae9e2d15171addf075290a7041aec008c0572f8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95ed6a5f-c6df-523f-b42e-cd835a9a1c8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb918b3042ca95c9401f2938258b7f13c909a87d18448c6e36c410a3d092dd94.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515188} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc82adce-c8de-5498-affa-bca1f361d52c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a3ed51c-6c18-5fdf-aaa4-d46ab866edd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-27537" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y=2{(\\frac{1}{7})}^{x}+3?$" :question/worked-solution "We start with plotting the graph of $y={(\\frac{1}{7})}^{x}:$\n\n![](images/75/75bb797ddbea41de97c1c4ba52e142342bfffb4f9b2b9b82111ebc94abf55446.png)\n\nNext, we plot the graph of $y=2{(\\frac{1}{7})}^{x}.$ To do this, we scale the graph above by a factor of $2.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,2)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/d6/d68957038bfad7dfb4547d69abd178b087dde6c0f7c8ba95aa0fcd7547ccebe6.png)\n\nFinally, we plot the graph of $y=2{(\\frac{1}{7})}^{x}+3.$ To do this, we shift the above graph $3$ units up. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,2)$ to $(0,5)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=3.$\n\n![](images/fb/fb918b3042ca95c9401f2938258b7f13c909a87d18448c6e36c410a3d092dd94.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320777af-ae37-523c-bacf-e28e66480cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514983} {:answer/id #uuid "7852e317-6684-5e8f-b211-c3d2fd1b2920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515122} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdb3a18-70b7-5be8-85e6-7d754574d6e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515204} {:answer/id #uuid "bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515274} {:answer/id #uuid "d551241c-84d6-5150-94ac-c0e6751dcdf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd2ebd72-45b1-5c05-82b9-a266f54fe224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515274} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3819eb9-9cd0-5d3c-852e-6d38178d3c62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "57c74959-06e0-5008-b9fc-e618f65747e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-143584" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{23}{15},$ find $\\text{E}[3X-Y].$" :question/worked-solution "We're given $\\text{E}[Y].$ So, we first need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nThe marginal density function for $X$ when $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{2}{9}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(2{x}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot \\frac{4}{9}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{4}+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(\\frac{1}{5}+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[3X-Y] & =3\\,\\text{E}[X]+(-1)\\,\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =3\\,(\\frac{8}{15})-(\\frac{23}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0506ec88-a559-5e5a-a458-6fc52ef5c6ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514885} {:answer/id #uuid "3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515001} {:answer/id #uuid "49850079-8fcd-5314-a588-f2594bdc6cde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515034} {:answer/id #uuid "53c3616a-163e-56aa-81e3-423c9687314d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515054} {:answer/id #uuid "fa17c92e-61ad-528a-bb3c-cafbd0c254a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3acf24ec-8a67-54b8-9448-b5fcd88660d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515001} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffe4c3f0-bc0e-50f0-bcdc-1b3ec7c8a111" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6838f2f1-19a5-5913-bfcd-14e938b0311d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143902" :question/problem "Three bags, $A,B,$ and $C,$ contain marbles. Bag $A$ contains $12$ red and $8$ green marbles, while bag $B$ contains $14$ red and $6$ green marbles. A bag is selected at random, and a marble is randomly selected from the bag. If the probability that the selected marble is green is $\\frac{2}{5},$  what proportion of marbles from bag $C$ are green?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event of selecting a green marble at random from one of the three bags, and \n\n- let $A$ be the event that the marble is from bag $A,$\n\n- let $B$ be the event that the marble is from bag $B,$\n\n- let $C$ be the event that the marble is from bag $C.$\n\nThen the disjoint union $A⊔B⊔C$ covers the entire sample space. \n\nTo calculate the probability of selecting a green marble, we can use the law of total probability: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G\\cap A)+P(G\\cap B)+P(G\\cap C) \\\\  & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each piece of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since a bag is selected at random, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(B)=P(C)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since there are $8$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $A,$ and  $6$ green marbles out of $20$  in bag $B,$ we have \n\n$$\nP(G|A)=\\frac{8}{20},\\,P(G|B)=\\frac{6}{20}.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability of picking a green marble  from one of the bags is $\\frac{2}{5},$ we have\n\n$$\nP(G)=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(G|C),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|B)P(B)+P(G|C)P(C) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =(\\frac{8}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{6}{20})(\\frac{1}{3})+P(G|C)(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2}{15}+\\frac{1}{10}+(\\frac{1}{3})P(G|C) \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{15}-\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ P(G|C) & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{1}{2}$ of the marbles from bag $C$ are green."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a4049a-fca7-5f52-bfb1-771580341b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514910} {:answer/id #uuid "15ccd49d-999f-5394-bd85-dc0b8b867ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514919} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd04e6e-2a4a-5265-b550-0dcfb916da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} {:answer/id #uuid "4ace196d-01ef-57ff-8b7f-750161ecd9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515038} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e6f4e6-23c8-5da2-a89b-5234a110c448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd04e6e-2a4a-5265-b550-0dcfb916da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3c01d9-f6b5-59af-9a9b-7d7b991856a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cac54f6-b1ee-5704-8eb2-39e7e0d78de0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95893" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overbrace{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)}^{g(x)}}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10528982-819d-558d-b7b9-c606e71872b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=3x+1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514906} {:answer/id #uuid "7d86ddc1-2c7d-548c-9b05-047b8457b098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=x-1\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515131} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e89105-6501-5255-9bbc-617aef43299e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=x-\\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515228} {:answer/id #uuid "becf689a-2251-5072-95a8-008d1c2e4200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=2x+\\pi\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515277} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=2x\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0b5a29-3a47-5678-8b2a-9278853cd35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=2x\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515373} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d670d1-3bff-5409-be4d-e79488473006" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae3534f1-44d3-55be-bcdb-7634e16c97c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132594" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Given that the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=2x{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=\\pi .$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =2(\\frac{1}{2}){e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi /2)}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1/2,\\pi )}(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z-1 & =2(x-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ z & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=\\pi \\\\ z &=2x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53cfc804-f2be-5e9c-8d5c-d7bbbd137c44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515056} :answer-field/id #uuid "029ce416-5248-5a5e-a914-f27e3f878e0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c20fd0ed-71f4-5fd0-a6bc-687a270c962b" :question/math-academy-id "q-333060" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}$ ,$\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\} &=L\\{4{x}_{1}(t)-3\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\} &=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0) &=4L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-3L\\{1\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0) &=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 &=4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1 &=-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\},$ and we have used the fact that $L\\{1\\}=\\frac{1}{s}.$\n\nNow, solving the first equation for ${X}_{1}(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-2 & =4{X}_{1}(s)-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =2-\\frac{3}{s} \\\\ (s-4){X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s} \\\\ {X}_{1}(s) & =\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this in the second equation and solving for ${X}_{2}(s),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{2}(s)+1 & =-{X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-{X}_{1}(s)-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =-(\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)})-1 \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-(2s-3)-s(s-4)}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-2s+3-{s}^{2}+4s}{s(s-4)} \\\\ (s-2){X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-4)} \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution of the new system in terms of parameter $s$ is \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2s-3}{s(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{-{s}^{2}+2s+3}{s(s-2)(s-4)}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cface83-381b-58c3-895b-8f62b382825c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515850} {:answer/id #uuid "7926303a-e2b6-5159-985f-0ad46e76f612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515875} {:answer/id #uuid "9fee32d0-78da-51c3-a53c-1e137107d56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515886} {:answer/id #uuid "a238cdeb-c29f-50a9-a436-52e309bee941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{37}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515887} {:answer/id #uuid "cf1d0da7-26e6-50bb-81f0-8728aeea07aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{39}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cface83-381b-58c3-895b-8f62b382825c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515850} :answer-field/id #uuid "a920c61e-b853-5722-89c4-a929b87344b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "449a125e-7ab5-525b-be8a-783acbe8eade" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{5}{3},$ then $2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+10\\pi )+9=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8e7894ea970c539ca59a73713fa15450f4361b3fc8bc22183e3fe84946411bd.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. This means that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is an *odd* function, and we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x)=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+10\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 5) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the oddness of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x) & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(-x+10\\pi )+9 & =2(-\\frac{5}{3})+9 \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{3}+9 \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e7552e-d725-5417-a68a-a0ae59981eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516017} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3ab759-1066-5e55-8d26-55227899a270" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516027} {:answer/id #uuid "74aca53e-2b6e-5cf2-80e1-85f44058d36d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3 \\pi}{2} -\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516047} {:answer/id #uuid "a8190e44-0a31-5cad-949d-3eb67a9b3a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516057} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8fc8f4-28cd-5883-b7c0-2ffa7f93f126" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8190e44-0a31-5cad-949d-3eb67a9b3a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516057} :answer-field/id #uuid "01de9f52-04ef-5589-ae8c-78fc75067ee6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "47728796-a73f-5a89-9d45-f02158bf0e21" :question/problem "If $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x+3\\pi )-3.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x=\\tan (x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\tan x=\\tan (x+3\\cdot \\pi )=\\tan (x+3\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get that $\\tan (x+3\\pi )=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x+3\\pi )-3=-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-3=\\frac{1}{4}-3=-\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "739b350e-bbb9-5c67-9578-e344455fb9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516046} {:answer/id #uuid "96d2e11b-86af-5028-9458-0a6a6ae93d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516055} {:answer/id #uuid "c9642556-a1ac-5918-9e65-d37291107c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516068} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b95482-9964-5776-bd40-5534c46d1393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516074} {:answer/id #uuid "df37ab9d-6f95-56d6-827a-f0508d58aa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4} + 2 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "739b350e-bbb9-5c67-9578-e344455fb9ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516046} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4c5fa3-faed-5373-bd78-453ec3fe0534" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aeda97fe-9fca-505e-9630-cba6d1c30202" :question/problem "If $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x-4\\pi )-4.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x=\\tan (x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\tan x=\\tan (x+(-4)\\cdot \\pi )=\\tan (x-4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get that $\\tan (x-4\\pi )=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x-4\\pi )-4=-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-4=\\frac{1}{4}-4=-\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d4b94a-7aaa-53d3-a495-fdf7a5bcb771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516022} {:answer/id #uuid "149eae0a-85d5-5d08-ae12-c600829558cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516023} {:answer/id #uuid "5e05a20e-26d7-5c89-9828-83880164edfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4} + \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516039} {:answer/id #uuid "d26ff6c9-9b2b-54ea-b214-7b5387abf4df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516071} {:answer/id #uuid "e3df34b7-9895-56b6-85e8-20965eb637ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11d4b94a-7aaa-53d3-a495-fdf7a5bcb771" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516022} :answer-field/id #uuid "baed5a1a-bd9f-5ecd-98e4-2bb6c9ee2a21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516065}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ca9d2be8-e824-5407-9b93-c123211be8a7" :question/problem "If $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x-2\\pi )-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\tan x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\tan x=\\tan (x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\tan x=\\tan (x+(-2)\\cdot \\pi )=\\tan (x-2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get that $\\tan (x-2\\pi )=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\tan (x-2\\pi )-2=-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2})-2=\\frac{1}{4}-2=-\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516077 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d65e09-d83b-5ffa-aa9d-1ea0ba977f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516019} {:answer/id #uuid "0f46a1af-c913-5917-bae1-eed6f2f672c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi}{2} -\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516020} {:answer/id #uuid "44b09449-d86f-5084-aa60-1b974bcb9287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516034} {:answer/id #uuid "97362675-915e-57fc-86cc-e8c93dea057e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516056} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fad3fe-6e88-5122-8df3-9d6106ea3bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2fad3fe-6e88-5122-8df3-9d6106ea3bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186